    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Four cotton strips protected in stainless steel mesh tea diffusers were deployed in the riverbed surface at 48 sites by 2-person teams in multiple rivers within the Yakima River Basin during the week of July 25-28, 2022 and were retrieved during the week of August 8-12, 2022. After retrieval, strips were gently cleaned in stream water, preserved in 70% ethanol, and processed to measure tensile strength loss as a proxy for decomposition rates. Decomposition rates were calculated per chronological days (Kcd) and per cumulative degree days (Kdd). Statistical analyses included ordinary least squares regression to examine univariate correlations between decay rates and ecosystem respiration components, multiple regression for optimized explanatory models, and LASSO regression using physical, chemical, and environmental variables."
    ],
